; equality_grows_past_the_index_width: an index of i64::MAX is charged as a
; growth, not clamped away, so the fault is the budget's and not the target's.
;
; EQUALITY grows the model to cover the largest index it was handed, and the
; needed size is that index plus one. At i64::MAX that addition overflows the
; charge width. Rust used to clamp the overflow to zero, which charged
; nothing, passed the size range check on a size of zero and fell through to
; IndexOutOfBounds, while xqvm_py computed 2^63 from unbounded integers,
; charged (2^63 - size) * 8 bytes and raised MemoryLimitExceeded. Same
; bytecode, the 1 GiB default budget this vector runs at, two fault
; identities -- the divergence narrowing the index used to cause, surviving
; on the one index value where the arithmetic itself overflows.
;
; The overflow now clamps up, to i64::MAX, one variable short of Python's
; 2^63. The charge cannot see the difference: both cost more than four times
; a u64 and are refused for that reason rather than by comparison against
; any particular budget. MemoryLimitExceeded is therefore the answer at
; every budget a host can express, which is what this vector pins.

PUSH 1
BQMX r0
VECI r1
VECI r2
PUSH 9223372036854775807
VECPUSH r1
PUSH 1
VECPUSH r2
PUSH 1
PUSH 1
EQUALITY r0 r1 r2
HALT
